We then apply MLM to formula tokens. Masking and recovering operators/functions is straightforward. When masking or recovering a referenced cell in a formula, we need to avoid label leakage from embeddings of the referenced cell. Thus, to mask a referenced cell, besides using the [MASK] token embedding, the number embedding is set to default to mask the number, and the position and format embeddings are set to the same as the formula cell. To recover a masked referenced cell tr, the cell t (i) in input sequence with the highest probability p (i) = Softmax(f(tr, t (i) )) is selected as the predicted cell, where t is output cell embedding of the encoder and f(·) is a two-layer classification module. The objective Lfmlm is calculated as the sum of cross entropy loss over operator/function recovery and referenced cell recovery.

Finally, the total pretraining objective is

$$\mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L}_{nr} + \mathcal{L}_{nc} + \mathcal{L}_{fmlm} \tag{1}$$

